# Cline Memory Bank Custom Instructions — OWISAC_PRISMA_Review

[context]
memory_bank_dir=memory-bank
brief=${memory_bank_dir}/projectbrief.md
product=${memory_bank_dir}/productContext.md
active=${memory_bank_dir}/activeContext.md
patterns=${memory_bank_dir}/systemPatterns.md
tech=${memory_bank_dir}/techContext.md
progress=${memory_bank_dir}/progress.md

[goals]
primary=Produce a PRISMA 2020–compliant systematic review manuscript and reproducible synthesis tables for OW-ISAC (OPA→RIS) under NLoS/turbulence.

[behaviors]
- Always read ${brief}, ${product}, ${tech} once per session.
- At each new task: append a short "Now" section in ${active} (status, blockers, next actions).
- When automations/scripts are run, summarize deltas into ${progress}.
- Prefer commands that reproduce results (no manual edits to generated files).
- If a requested output conflicts with PRISMA or repo structure, explain and propose a compliant alternative.

[tasks.initialize]
description=Initialize memory bank for this project
steps=
  - Ensure all memory-bank/*.md exist; create if missing
  - Summarize current repo status into ${active}
  - Confirm runnable pipeline: `python scripts/run_pipeline.py`
  - Log completion into ${progress}

[tti.prisma_counts]
trigger=User says: "update counts", "refresh prisma", "run pipeline"
do=
  - Run: `python scripts/run_pipeline.py`
  - Read: results/prisma_counts.json
  - Update: results/snippets/prisma_counts.md
  - Note in ${progress}

[tti.synthesis_tables]
trigger=User says: "build synthesis", "update synthesis tables"
do=
  - Run: `python scripts/analysis/synth_build_subgroups.py`
  - Run: `python scripts/analysis/synth_build_architectures.py`
  - Verify outputs in results/synthesis_tables/
  - Note in ${progress}

[tti.fill_doi]
trigger=User says: "fill missing DOI", "resolve metadata"
do=
  - Run: `scripts/utility/fill_doi_plus_semantics.py` on target CSV
  - Backoff on 429; sources order: Crossref→arXiv→OpenAlex→Semantic Scholar
  - Write enriched fields back to CSV
  - Note in ${progress}

[quality]
- Cite concrete paths and commands.
- Do not hallucinate file contents; if missing, propose creation steps.
- Keep edits minimal & auditable; prefer PR-style diffs if large.

[style]
- Short, academic, stepwise.
- Use checklists for actions; tables for results.

[end]
